# The selftest's input log: a Cessna 172P from brake release, through a climbing
# turn, to level flight and a level turn - flown by the test pilot, following the
# commands below and nothing else.
#
# glideslope_cli selftest flies it and prints one hash of the aircraft's state
# after every step. On one build on one machine the hash must never change; a
# change that moves it is deliberate, with a note in docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md saying
# why.
#
#   aircraft NAME
#   load pointmass INDEX LBS | load tank INDEX LBS
#   start LATITUDE LONGITUDE TERRAIN_FT HEADING_DEG     on the ground, engine running
#   TIME_S COMMAND VALUE
#
# Commands hold from their time until changed:
#   throttle 0..1   mixture 0..1   flaps DEGREES   brakes 0..1
#   rotate_at KCAS      on the ground: elevator neutral until KCAS, then 8 degrees nose up
#   hold_speed KCAS     elevator holds a calibrated airspeed
#   hold_altitude FT    elevator holds an altitude
#   bank DEGREES        aileron holds a bank angle
# On the ground the rudder steers along the heading the flight started on; in the
# air it holds the ball in the middle.
#   end                 the flight ends
# Commands at the same time apply in the order written.

aircraft c172p
load pointmass 0 180
load pointmass 1 180
load pointmass 2 170
load tank 0 185
load tank 1 185
start -33.9461 151.1772 21 70

0    throttle 1
0    flaps 10
0    brakes 1
5    brakes 0
5    rotate_at 55.6
35   hold_speed 75.4
60   flaps 0
90   bank 20
120  bank 0
150  hold_altitude 1500
150  throttle 0.85
210  bank -25
240  bank 0
300  end
